hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"21403","Yahya ibn Saeed narrated to us: Hisham ibn Urwah informed us: my father informed us: Abu Ayyub informed me that Ubayy narrated to him, saying: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: A man has intercourse with his wife but does not ejaculate. He said: He washes what touched the woman of him, performs ablution, and prays."
"21404","Abdullah narrated to us, saying: my father narrated to me, saying: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, saying: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us from his father from Abu Ayyub from Ubayy ibn Kab who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned its meaning."
"21405","He said: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us from Hisham ibn Urwah, saying: my father narrated to me from al-Malli, from al-Malli, meaning by his saying al-Malli, from al-Malli, Abu Ayyub, from Ubayy ibn Kab from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning one who comes to his wife then does not ejaculate: He washes his private part and performs ablution. Abdullah said: my father said: al-Malli from al-Malli is trustworthy from trustworthy."
"21406","Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to me, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us from Hisham ibn Urwah from his father, saying: A hadith from Abu Ayyub ibn Zayd reached me while he was in the land of Rum, so I met Abu Ayyub and he narrated to me from Ubayy ibn Kab that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man has intercourse with his wife then is sluggish, let him wash what touched the woman of him, then let him perform ablution."
